# Software-project request phrase vocabulary (issues #1138, #1175).
#
# The object-phrase discipline of rust/src/solver_handlers/
# software_project_phrases.rs reads every surface from this file — the words
# that close an authoring verb's object noun phrase (so the artifact kind is
# the head the verb governs, never an incidental modifier), the determiners
# and benefactives that may lead the phrase without belonging to it, and the
# punctuation that ends a phrase or a sentence. The recognition algorithm is
# compiled; the vocabulary is data, one meaning per table, so extending the
# languages covered needs no Rust change. Every record is defined by the
# statement function-word genus — these surfaces carry grammatical structure,
# not lexical content.

